<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="semattor_shelfsense" translate="label" sortOrder="900" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
            <label>ShelfSense Sorting</label>
            <tab>catalog</tab>
            <resource>Semattor_ShelfSense::config</resource>
            <group id="general" translate="label" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                <label>General</label>
                <comment>ShelfSense Sorting version 1.6.0. See CHANGELOG.md in the module folder.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Only changes categories where you chose something other than "Standard". Other categories are never touched.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="cron_expr" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Night run time (cron)</label>
                    <comment>Default: 15 3 * * * (03:15). The night run only re-sorts categories that are due (see next field). When you save a category, its order is updated right away.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="interval_days" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="22" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Re-sort every X days</label>
                    <comment>Default 2. A higher number means less work for the server and fewer changes for search and feeds. Applies to all options, also Auto.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="own_brand_first" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="23" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Own brand first</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>All options except Standard show our own brand before other brands. Other brands come after them. In a category without own brand products, the other brands are sorted as usual. Pinned SKUs still come first.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="test_place" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="23" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Test products start on place</label>
                    <comment>Default 5. Test products set on a category are shown from this place until their end date.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="own_brands" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="24" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Own brand names</label>
                    <comment>Exact name(s) in the Brand attribute, separated by commas. Default: SE Mattor</comment>
                    <depends><field id="own_brand_first">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="brand_attribute" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="24" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Brand attribute code</label>
                    <comment>Default: brand</comment>
                    <depends><field id="own_brand_first">1</field></depends>
                </field>
                <field id="top_count" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="25" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Sort the top X products</label>
                    <comment>Default 300. These get an exact new order. The products after them keep their old order (sold out last). This keeps the work small for big categories, because the products further down almost never move. 0 = sort all products.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="out_of_stock_last" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Sold out products last</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="bestseller" translate="label" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Best sellers</label>
                <field id="days" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Count sales from the last X days</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="auto" translate="label comment" sortOrder="25" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Auto (learning)</label>
                <comment>Auto learns from what customers see, click and buy in each category, and tests new products in a few places. It can be chosen on a category when enough data is collected.</comment>
                <field id="tracking" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Collect views and clicks</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Counts which products customers see and click in category lists. No personal data is stored, only numbers per day.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="sample_rate" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="15" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Measure X% of category page views</label>
                    <comment>Default 50. Each measured page sends one small request when the customer leaves the page. Lower = less server load, but Auto needs more days to learn.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-digits-range digits-range-1-100</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="min_days" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Days of data needed before Auto can be chosen</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="min_views" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Product views needed before Auto can be chosen</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="exploration" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Testing share (%)</label>
                    <comment>Share of the top places used to test products Auto knows little about. Default 15.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-digits-range digits-range-0-50</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="window_days" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Learn from the last X days</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="min_product_views" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="60" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Views before a product counts as known</label>
                    <comment>Products with fewer views are tested in the testing places.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="smart" translate="label comment" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Most relevant (smart)</label>
                <comment>Score = sales (recent sales count double) + new product boost + your own position numbers. The weights are relative to each other, for example 50 / 25 / 25.</comment>
                <field id="weight_sales" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Weight: sales</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="weight_new" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Weight: new product</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="weight_manual" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Weight: your position numbers</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="new_half_life_days" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>New product boost halves every X days</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
                <field id="trend_days" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Recent sales window (days)</label>
                    <comment>Sales in this window count double.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
